{:edb/db-before-t 2708 :edb/db-after-t 2709 :edb/tx-data [[13194139536021 50 #inst "2026-10-09T13:05:16.714Z" 13194139536021 true] [17592186198291 1020 #edb/ref 17592186379716 13194139536021 true] [17592186198291 1020 #edb/ref 17592186379723 13194139536021 true] [17592186198333 1020 #edb/ref 17592186379730 13194139536021 true] [17592186198581 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536021 true] [17592186198581 1100 "The lamina $D = {(x, y): 0 \\le x \\le \\sin y, 0 \\le y \\le \\frac{π}{2}}$ has the mass density function $λ(x, y) = 6\\cos y$. Find the moment of the lamina about the $y$-axis." 13194139536021 false] [17592186198581 1100 "The lamina $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡y,\\,0\\le y\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}}$ has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=6\\operatorname{cos}⁡y.$ Find the moment of the lamina about the $y$-axis." 13194139536021 true] [17592186198581 1145 "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{y}={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is represented as a type II plane region and $\\lambda (x,y)=6\\operatorname{cos}⁡y.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}x\\cdot 6\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}6x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡y}6x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡y[{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡y}2x\\,\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\cdot {[{x}^{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}3{sin}^{2}⁡y\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[{sin}^{3}⁡y]}_{y=0}^{y=\\pi /2} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536021 true] [17592186198893 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536021 true] [17592186198893 1100 "Consider the thin plate $D$ enclosed between the curve $y = 4 - x^{2}$ and the $x$-axis for $-2 \\le x \\le 2$. Given that the area of the plate is $\\frac{32}{3}$, find the $y$-coordinate of its centroid." 13194139536021 false] [17592186198893 1100 "Consider the thin plate $D$ enclosed between the curve $y=4-{x}^{2}$ and the $x$-axis for $-2\\le x\\le 2.$ Given that the area of the plate is $\\frac{32}{3},$ find the $y$-coordinate of its centroid." 13194139536021 true] [17592186198893 1145 "The centroid of a lamina $D$ with area ${A}_{D}$ is given by $({x}_{c},{y}_{c}),$ where\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}=\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}x\\,\\,\\text{d}A,\\,{y}_{c}=\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}y\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type I plane region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073832/assets/536f542f535513430311b29f43f6fbafb37832d6dfde3b9c81e82237cb011821.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 4-{x}^{2}}\n$$\n\nand ${A}_{D}=\\frac{32}{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-coordinate of the centroid is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{c} & =\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}y\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{32}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{4-{x}^{2}}y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{32}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=4-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{64}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}(16-8{x}^{2}+{x}^{4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{64}{[16x-\\frac{8{x}^{3}}{3}+\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}]}_{-2}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{64}[(32-\\frac{64}{3}+\\frac{32}{5})-(-32+\\frac{64}{3}-\\frac{32}{5})] \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536021 true] [17592186379716 1017 #edb/ref 17592186379717 13194139536021 true] [17592186379716 1089 "q-163165" 13194139536021 true] [17592186379716 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536021 true] [17592186379716 1100 "Consider the lamina that occupies the region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{x}}$ and has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=y.$ Given that the mass of the lamina is $\\frac{9}{4}$ units and its center of mass is located at $(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y}),$ what is the value of $\\overset{―}{x}?$" 13194139536021 true] [17592186379716 1113 #uuid "e02f0f42-c179-5b96-a0d2-43d791b3159e" 13194139536021 true] [17592186379716 1145 "The center of mass of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ is given by \n\n$$\n(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y})=(\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m},\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n- $m={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$ is the mass of the lamina,\n\n- ${M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\\,$ is the moment of the lamina about the $x$-axis, and\n\n- ${M}_{y}={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$ is the moment of the lamina about the $y$-axis.\n\nSince we require the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass, we need to compute the moment about the $y$-axis: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}x\\cdot y\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}xy\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}x[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}y\\,\\text{d}y]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}x{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}x(\\frac{x}{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}]}_{x=0}^{x=3} \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m}=\\frac{(\\frac{9}{2})}{(\\frac{9}{4})}=2.\n$$" 13194139536021 true] [17592186379717 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379718 13194139536021 true] [17592186379717 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379719 13194139536021 true] [17592186379717 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379720 13194139536021 true] [17592186379717 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379721 13194139536021 true] [17592186379717 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379722 13194139536021 true] [17592186379717 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536021 true] [17592186379717 1041 "selection" 13194139536021 true] [17592186379717 1104 #edb/ref 17592186379719 13194139536021 true] [17592186379717 1110 #uuid "f44f0551-ec9b-5088-aa7c-af9998737a11" 13194139536021 true] [17592186379718 1034 "\\frac{5}{2}" 13194139536021 true] [17592186379718 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536021 true] [17592186379718 1111 #uuid "bee81527-aad8-5537-b851-0540e9645abe" 13194139536021 true] [17592186379719 1034 "2" 13194139536021 true] [17592186379719 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536021 true] [17592186379719 1111 #uuid "6f786f97-657d-5994-8fa2-66d1cfcb6cce" 13194139536021 true] [17592186379720 1034 "\\frac{4}{3}" 13194139536021 true] [17592186379720 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536021 true] [17592186379720 1111 #uuid "1696dac9-b3e7-5c0a-a719-1b35e0eb2695" 13194139536021 true] [17592186379721 1034 "1" 13194139536021 true] [17592186379721 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536021 true] [17592186379721 1111 #uuid "46c9d132-a2c9-5e56-8e9d-4ddcdb375e06" 13194139536021 true] [17592186379722 1034 "\\frac{3}{2}" 13194139536021 true] [17592186379722 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536021 true] [17592186379722 1111 #uuid "c33f22d2-1344-5021-9d50-0f0c94166c8a" 13194139536021 true] [17592186379723 1017 #edb/ref 17592186379724 13194139536021 true] [17592186379723 1089 "q-163280" 13194139536021 true] [17592186379723 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536021 true] [17592186379723 1100 "Consider a thin plate $D$ that has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)={x}^{3}$ and is enclosed between the curve $y=x$ and the $x$-axis for $0\\le x\\le 2.$ Given that the mass of the plate is $\\frac{32}{5}$ units and its center of mass is located at $(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y}),$ what is the value of $\\overset{―}{y}?$" 13194139536021 true] [17592186379723 1113 #uuid "b621632e-572a-5d85-9322-247a4902c63b" 13194139536021 true] [17592186379723 1145 "The center of mass of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ is given by \n\n$$\n(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y})=(\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m},\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n- $m={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$ is the mass of the lamina,\n\n- ${M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\\,$ is the moment of the lamina about the $x$-axis, and\n\n- ${M}_{y}={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$ is the moment of the lamina about the $y$-axis.\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type I plane region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073832/assets/a042919f73d668cac20ead2752c689e57880f60bc096747f41cec3aeb3ed62ca.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le x}\n$$\n\nand $\\lambda (x,y)={x}^{3}.$ \n\nSince we require the $y$-coordinate of the center of mass, we need to compute the moment about the $x$-axis: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}y{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}y{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{3}[{\\int }_{0}^{x}y\\,\\text{d}y]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{3}\\cdot {[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{12}{x}^{6}]}_{x=0}^{x=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}\\cdot 64 \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}=\\frac{(\\frac{16}{3})}{(\\frac{32}{5})}=\\frac{5}{6}.\n$$" 13194139536021 true] [17592186379724 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379725 13194139536021 true] [17592186379724 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379726 13194139536021 true] [17592186379724 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379727 13194139536021 true] [17592186379724 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379728 13194139536021 true] [17592186379724 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379729 13194139536021 true] [17592186379724 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536021 true] [17592186379724 1041 "selection" 13194139536021 true] [17592186379724 1104 #edb/ref 17592186379725 13194139536021 true] [17592186379724 1110 #uuid "daab8ee5-e1f1-5751-98b7-f8f0f0fb58bb" 13194139536021 true] [17592186379725 1034 "\\frac{5}{6}" 13194139536021 true] [17592186379725 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536021 true] [17592186379725 1111 #uuid "9f2c162d-ab9c-542b-b6d2-f6ca84e19dac" 13194139536021 true] [17592186379726 1034 "\\frac{3}{5}" 13194139536021 true] [17592186379726 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536021 true] [17592186379726 1111 #uuid "e1eb803a-62d5-5e80-8382-2d440d50ca64" 13194139536021 true] [17592186379727 1034 "\\frac{4}{3}" 13194139536021 true] [17592186379727 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536021 true] [17592186379727 1111 #uuid "fdad9559-c900-5c08-9238-937147ae3813" 13194139536021 true] [17592186379728 1034 "\\frac{3}{2}" 13194139536021 true] [17592186379728 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536021 true] [17592186379728 1111 #uuid "0e04f94c-6f07-5832-a020-963c15980bfc" 13194139536021 true] [17592186379729 1034 "\\frac{16}{15}" 13194139536021 true] [17592186379729 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536021 true] [17592186379729 1111 #uuid "219a7f94-bd61-58b2-b8f6-bb86fb58ae4a" 13194139536021 true] [17592186379730 1017 #edb/ref 17592186379731 13194139536021 true] [17592186379730 1089 "q-163584" 13194139536021 true] [17592186379730 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536021 true] [17592186379730 1100 "A thin plate $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{y}{x}$ is enclosed between the line $x=y$ and the line $x=1$ for $1\\le y\\le 2.$ Find the moment of the plate about the $y$-axis." 13194139536021 true] [17592186379730 1113 #uuid "dabea3df-197a-52a6-8580-bad2eb26b411" 13194139536021 true] [17592186379730 1145 "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{y}={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is a type II plane region, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073832/assets/6cfa58d15b2a1f05aa4d4d088d44b44d6b3225084f627bc8078617d85d801957.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le y,\\,1\\le y\\le 2}\n$$\n\nand $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{y}{x}.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}x\\cdot \\frac{y}{x}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}y\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{y}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}y[{\\int }_{1}^{y}\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}y[x]_{x=1}^{x=y}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}y(y-1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{y}^{2}-y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{y=1}^{y=2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{8}{3}-2)-(\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536021 true] [17592186379731 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379732 13194139536021 true] [17592186379731 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379733 13194139536021 true] [17592186379731 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379734 13194139536021 true] [17592186379731 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379735 13194139536021 true] [17592186379731 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379736 13194139536021 true] [17592186379731 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536021 true] [17592186379731 1041 "selection" 13194139536021 true] [17592186379731 1104 #edb/ref 17592186379732 13194139536021 true] [17592186379731 1110 #uuid "15aa6e40-8ab8-50a6-867b-e5d5d575be22" 13194139536021 true] [17592186379732 1034 "\\frac{5}{6}" 13194139536021 true] [17592186379732 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536021 true] [17592186379732 1111 #uuid "01eef2d9-afa7-515b-8818-9d40657e72b9" 13194139536021 true] [17592186379733 1034 "\\frac{4}{3}" 13194139536021 true] [17592186379733 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536021 true] [17592186379733 1111 #uuid "fb3f6f7c-5296-58bc-af2e-2e863311c6b8" 13194139536021 true] [17592186379734 1034 "\\frac{7}{6}" 13194139536021 true] [17592186379734 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536021 true] [17592186379734 1111 #uu